<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdurrauf of Singkil</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1615–<a href="/years/1693">1693</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Abdurrauf al-Singkili</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdurrauf of Singkil was a Malay Islamic scholar from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aceh">Aceh</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>. After about nineteen years of study in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> he returned around 1661 and served the queens of Aceh as their chief religious authority. He wrote the first commentary on the whole Qur'an in Malay and spread the Shattariyya <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> order in the Malay world.</p></div>
